    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1093">

                <pb facs="1350" n="1336" xml:id="pg1336"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">102.8951: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >White</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-04-19">April 19, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>387. For Rubber Development Losa<anchor n="57" xml:id="d1093-f1"/> from
                        Truslow.<anchor n="58" xml:id="d1093-f2"/> RDC rubber agreement with Peru
                    terminates December 31, 1946.<anchor n="59" xml:id="d1093-f3"/> The price
                    premium agreement terminates March 31, 1946.<anchor n="60" xml:id="d1093-f4"/>
                </p>
                <p>[Here follow paragraphs the same, <hi rendition="#italic">mutatis mutandis</hi>,
                    as in telegram 1000 of the same date to Rio de Janeiro, printed on <ref
                        target="#pg704">page 704</ref>.]</p>
                <p>A similar proposal is being presented to each other American country
                    participating in rubber program.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed> [Truslow] <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1093-f1" n="57" xml:id="d1093-f1-content">
                <p>Otto Losa, Special representative of the Rubber Development Corporation.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1093-f2" n="58" xml:id="d1093-f2-content">
                <p>Francis A. Truslow, President, Rubber Development Corporation.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1093-f3" n="59" xml:id="d1093-f3-content">
                <p>Agreement signed April 23, 1942, not printed; for negotiations, see <ref
                        target="frus1942v06#pg_665">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1942, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">vi</hi>, pp. 665</ref>–<ref
                        target="frus1942v06#pg_670">670</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1093-f4" n="60" xml:id="d1093-f4-content">
                <p>The agreement between the Rubber Development Corporation and the Peruvian Amazon
                    Corporation (not printed) was made by an exchange of letters dated February 16
                    and 25, 1944, and extended by a similar exchange of August 25 and 29, 1944. It
                    effected a 33½% price increase.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
